  "id": "COMPOUND:25760 - PROTEIN:917",
  "verbalization": "Sikokianin A is implicated in the activation of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2A through a series of molecular pathways involving the serine/threonine-protein kinases Nek9, Ulk2, and MAPK kinase kinase 13, all of which are targets of Phytolaccoside B. This suggests a potential mechanism where Sikokianin A may modulate signaling through these kinases, ultimately influencing the activity of the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2A. The evidence is consistent across three distinct pathways, each linking Sikokianin A to Phytolaccoside B, which in turn activates the receptor. The overlapping targets and the shared role of Phytolaccoside B as a common mediator highlight a potential convergent mechanism. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Sikokianin A exerts its effects via a kinase-mediated pathway that ultimately affects the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2A.",
